# Save a workout. Start the API with Aspire first, then send "Create an account" once.
@host = http://localhost:5279

### Create an account → 201. The requests below use its access token.
# @name createAccount
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user-{{$guid}}@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "timeZone": "Europe/Zagreb"
}

### An unknown workout → 404 workout.not_found. Use the ID of a workout in progress with a checked set to get a 200.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/workouts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "completed"
}

### Save with a name → 200 with the new name. Use the ID of a workout in progress with a checked set.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/workouts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "completed",
  "name": "Hotel gym"
}

### An empty name → 400 validation, with an error for name.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/workouts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "completed",
  "name": " "
}

### Any other status → 400 validation_failed.
PATCH {{host}}/api/v1/workouts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "skipped"
}
